{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall place the cover upon the ark from above, and into the ark you shall put the testimony which I shall give you.</b> For indeed the direction of the intellect toward discovery of universals and their abstraction from matter, and likewise its acceptance of them when it receives them so as to acquire them as a possession — all this arises for him through the medium of contemplation and practical preparations. If so, all this is attained by gazing upon the testimony that is in the ark, over which is the cover, for indeed in the testimony — which is the Decalogue — the universals of both the contemplative and the practical parts are to be found. And in this He promised."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:12.919935078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}